    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-human-rights-commission-amendment-costs-protection-act-2024-sch-1-sec-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "3 Section 46PSA",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-human-rights-commission-amendment-costs-protection-act-2024#sch-1-sec-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-human-rights-commission-amendment-costs-protection-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-human-rights-commission-amendment-costs-protection-act-2024.pdf, p.7",
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the section, substitute:\n46PSA  Costs\nScope\n(1) This section applies to proceedings (including an appeal) in a court\nthat relate to an application made by a person (the applicant) under\nsection 46PO in respect of one or more respondents to a terminated\ncomplaint.\nWhen respondent liable for costs\n(2) Subject to subsection (4), if the applicant is successful in\nproceedings on one or more grounds, the court must order each\nrespondent against whom the applicant is successful to pay the\napplicant’s costs.\n(3) The court may order that the costs to be paid by the respondent be\nassessed on an indemnity basis or otherwise.\n(4) If the court is satisfied that the applicant’s unreasonable act or\nomission caused the applicant to incur costs, the court is not\nrequired to order the respondent to pay the costs incurred as a\nresult of that act or omission.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments",
      "skos:definition": "Repeal the section, substitute:\n46PSA  Costs\nScope\n(1) This section applies to proceedings (including an appeal) in a court\nthat relate to an application made by a person (the applicant) under\nsection 46PO in respect of one or more respondents to a terminated\ncomplaint.\nWhen respondent liable for costs\n(2) Subject to subsection (4), if the applicant is successful in\nproceedings on one or more grounds, the court must order each\nrespondent against whom the applicant is successful to pay the\napplicant’s costs.\n(3) The court may order that the costs to be paid by the respondent be\nassessed on an indemnity basis or otherwise.\n(4) If the court is satisfied that the applicant’s unreasonable act or\nomission caused the applicant to incur costs, the court is not\nrequired to order the respondent to pay the costs incurred as a\nresult of that act or omission.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-human-rights-commission-amendment-costs-protection-act-2024-sch-1-sec-3-ss-1"
        },
